<!--
Example "checklist" cron job. Rename this file to checklist.md to activate it
(any cron/*.md is loaded and armed; a .example file is ignored).

Frontmatter:
  schedule  robfig/cron syntax: "@every 30m", "@daily", or a 5-field spec like
            "*/30 8-22 * * *" (every 30 min, 8am-10pm — active hours only).
  agent     a subagent from agents/ to run the checklist (here: assistant).
  direct    true posts the run's raw result straight to the chat, costing
            no agent turn. Leave it off for report-style jobs — the result
            then arrives as mail to the main agent, which messages you only
            when this run carries something worth saying. Failures always
            surface either way.

The body is the prompt. Write it to report findings plainly; the agent
stays silent on runs with nothing worth saying, so no sentinel is needed.
-->
---
schedule: "@every 30m"
agent: assistant
---
Periodic check-in. Work through the checklist with your tools. Each run is a
fresh conversation — if a check must not repeat, track its state in a file.

Checklist:
- Anything urgent on disk or in the running jobs that needs my human?

If something needs attention, reply with a concise alert and nothing else.
If nothing does, say briefly that all is quiet.
